<!-- PICK model: a copy of Fr3HGripperCarry/fr3_H_gripper_lite.xml with exactly two
     changes, both from pick_vs_carry_changes.md section 4.
       1. finger-pad friction 1.0/0.02/0.01 -> 2.0/0.05/0.02. The pads carry
          priority="3", so they override the box's own friction. Reason on record: the
          real pads do not slip but the simulated ones did.
       2. grab_motor forcerange +-10 N -> +-40 N. 10 N was the binding constraint when
          lifting 0.5 kg on two pad faces.
     kp/kv stay at 200/40, NOT the 1000 the document assumed. 200 was measured against
     the real gripper's closing latency, and raising it back would undo that. The
     consequence is arithmetic and worth knowing: at kp=200 a full close command
     (0.048 m of slide error) develops 200*0.048 = 9.6 N, so forcerange is no longer
     what limits grip force -- kp is. If more grip force is wanted, kp is the knob, and
     the closing time (roughly kv/kp) moves with it.
     Everything else, including the sugar_box definition, is byte-identical to Carry. -->
